    "name": "Apprentice Pewter Dampener",
    "description": "An early-tier apprentice dampening field, woven from rudimentary tallow threads and pulverized pewter. The Clockwork Deep-Bore Syndicate originally devised this whimsical 'gravel-pad' folk-logic to protect sensitive pneumatic pipes from their own explosive bore-charges. Laid over a quarry square, it intercepts 70% of stray secondary splash damage, saving the block below from an accidental cleave.",
